From 82a4655911824e962a19ae04ff1d67b5fcb3e9ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:07:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/timer: PDEC (U2263) position decoder

The PDEC as PIC32CM MC00 silicon showed it (firmware/hello
APP=pdecprobe and pdecprobe2, checked by pdec):

- Inputs from the PDEC pads (the generic pad input path, "pad-qdi-in")
  or events EVU0-2, with PINVEN/EVINV and SWAP. Input changes in one
  instant are decoded together, so one event into two inputs is a
  simultaneous change.
- QDEC and HALL wait for START after every enable; COUNTER runs from
  the enable. STOP keeps COUNT; RETRIGGER loads 0 in either direction.
- X4: the S0-leading order counts up, 4 per cycle; a reversal sets
  STATUS.DIR at its first edge and INTFLAG.DIR with VLC at the second;
  a simultaneous S0/S1 change sets QERR and ERR without counting,
  except the first transition after START. X2: S0 edges count, down
  while S1 is 1.
- COUNT's angular and revolution parts wrap at their TOPs (all ones or
  CC0's parts with PEREN); an angular wrap moves the revolution count
  silently, a full wrap raises OVF. MC0/MC1 flag COUNT arriving at
  CC0/CC1, and a match at START and RETRIGGER.
- COUNTER counts GCLK_PDEC / 2^PRESC up to 0xFFFF or CC0.
- HALL: the code in COUNT[2:0], direction by the 1-3-2-6-4-5 order,
  HERR on 0 and 7.
- COUNT reads the READSYNC copy; CCx reads CCBUFx while valid, a second
  CCBUFx write meanwhile is dropped; UPDATE and an overflow (unless
  LUPD) copy the buffers.

Not modelled: the index and the X4S/X2S index checks (silicon did not
follow the data sheet there), AUTOC, the HALL window and delay
counters, the input filter, COUNTER event actions.

qtest pic32cm-pdec-test: X4, X2, COUNTER, the CC buffer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
